{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488771-your-moments-of-awesome-epic-fails-tearful-sadness-and-noodle-incidents","id":1488771,"title":"Your Moments of Awesome, Epic Fails, Tearful Sadness and Noodle Incidents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-02T01:05:13-07:00","id":1488771,"title":"Your Moments of Awesome, Epic Fails, Tearful Sadness and Noodle Incidents","content":"The<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1487407-badass-splat-boasts#post1487407\"> Badass Splat Boasts</a> thread made me think of situations where those boasts would apply in-game, which in turn made me wonder: what were some of the most awesome, fun, sad or memorable moments in your game?<br /> This thread is meant to share retellings and for reminiscing about those crowning achievements that gave you goosebumps, those plumbing depths that made you facepalm or cry, and everything in between that stood out. Of course, it is also meant, in turn, to serve as inspiration for others.<br /> <br /> One of mine: a Hero was stalking the Dean, who was acting as a sort-of surrogate &quot;Baron&quot; for the local Beast community, and a quite new PC, who was a student, came into the scene. Due to observation stuff, to protect her from possible fallout, we needed her to appear frightened and not connected to the Dean and my PC, a local Irish mob member (which she'd never met). To support her acting scared, I had the 'brilliant' idea to support her - by scaring her with a Giant-sized Anakim with Looming Presence and an Intimidation roll, which, of course, turned out exceptional. This placed a lasting fear in the student which made cooperation <i>that much harder</i>, but hey, at least the scream was very convincing!<br /> <br /> Another: the very same Anakim had a pendant (and Specialty) in staring down people with a murderous glare. It worked really well - until the moment he met a Ventrue whose Ghoul he'd killed. Let's just say, this staring match went very much not in his favour, and he spent quite some time running errands for someone he shouldn't have liked quite that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T09:38:40-07:00","id":1488839,"title":"","content":"Can't remember the endowment but<br /> <br /> Was a les mysteres hunter In a mixed cell. My other players were from the Maleficarum and lucifuge (quite the team I know). We were fighting a werewolf on top of an abandoned building (we had underestimated his climbing ability). Luckily, we had pistols, each with 2 silver bullets (resources were low, this was lone werewolf, which had story importance for later). I missed 2 both shots, the MM hit one, and the lucifuge hit both his.<br /> <br /> But the bastard wasn't dead. We had literally nothing. Even with the aggravated damage we were gonna die. So I did the only logical thing. I started running, did my leap of faith endowment, and tackled it off the building. When we hit the ground, the motherfucker was dead, and my character was in the hospital for the damage caused as the werewolf had left nasty gashes on me during the fall","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T09:07:27-07:00","id":1489232,"title":"","content":"Glad to see that my little creation inspired you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T21:57:10-08:00","id":1499490,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-