 style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Since when is London a murder-free zone? What kind of history teachers do you kids have these days?&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;YOU WHO CHALLENGE ME, PREPARE FOR AGONY. WITH YOUR BROKEN BONES AND SPILLED BLOOD, I SHALL WRITE THE HOLY PROGRAMMING OF WAR. IF YOU WISH TO BECOME LIKE ME, STEP FORTH AND DRAW YOUR WEAPONS. IF NOT, GO BACK AND WEEP IN DEFEAT FOREVERMORE.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;As for me... send a telepathic message if you detect any assassins or whatever heading our way so I can dispose of them. Been itching to break some bones lately,&quot; Said Anthony.<br /> <br /> &quot;You break my bones every time we spar!&quot; Observed Noose. &quot;Does it not count?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Not really, because you take it like a champ. I wanna make someone beg for mercy again,&quot; Said Anthony as he cracked his knuckles noisily.<br /> <br /> &quot;Did you hear that? He called me a champion! Does that mean we're friends now?&quot; Smiled Noose in a most disconcerting but optimistic fashion.<br /> <br /> &quot;...sure, let's go with that,&quot; Accepted Anthony.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The shadowy figure does not reply, a frigid wind blows through the desolate playground, and the moon is now even closer.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Huntsman tries to move toward Matilda, but cannot even move past a few inches before collapsing. Its entire body has been molten and incinerated so thoroughly that it does not even have flesh anymore, only a wooden doll-like skeleton. Gordon makes his way toward the feeble and agonizing creature, licking his lips and rubbing his hands in anticipation. The Huntsman tries to wobble away, but lacks the muscles and ligaments to move properly and lets out a quiet, gurgling scream.<br /> <br /> Gordon picks up the Huntsman by the throat and makes the fey creature look him in the eyes. &quot;Any last words?&quot; He inquires in a jolly tone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, nooooo... are you going to kill me? I'm sooo scared...&quot; The Huntsman manages to pathetically cough.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nope! I'm going to make you wish you were dead, my <i>most exotic and delectable of meals!</i> Don't worry, no part of you will go to waste!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait, NO! Eat the soldiers, not me, PLEASE!&quot; The Huntsman is dragged into Gordon's ravenous, gaping maw. The horrid, abominable sight can only be described as the painting of Saturn Devouring His Son brought to life. Even the Rat Pack, having seen Arcadia and the Gentry, feel as though their grip on reality loosens ever so slightly from merely gazing upon the mockery of a smile that Gordon does as he goes about the grisly act.<br /> <br /> And after the blink of an eye, the Huntsman is gone. All the remaining toy soldiers look at Gordon, petrified with terror. Gordon gives Caesar a knowing and satisfied look, before staring at the enemies and raising his voice.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Fee-fi-fo-fum, </i><br /> <i>I smell the blood of an Englishman, </i><br /> <i>Be he alive, or be he dead, </i><br /> <i>I'll grind his bones to make my bread!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> All of the enemies immediately flee into the Thorns without looking back.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As always, Aria is lucid from the moment her dream starts. As always, she dreams of the night. Sometimes with a moon, sometimes without, sometimes with glittering stars, sometimes without. But not the sun, never that.<br /> <br /> Not the gloomy forest in which she met Cain, but something more familiar, a distorted facsimile of the campus near her office. The broad strokes are correct, but as with all things dream, distances are wrong, proportions are wrong, and... purely out of her own habit, no one else is to be seen. Aria almost always dreams of alone.<br /> <br /> Clad in night and shadow, she looks skyward, and sweeps clouds aside to reveal the disc of Luna, an inverted mirror of the black hollow on her moonlight-paled face. A pretty sight, but not what she needs in this moment. Drawing a classroom prism from her pocket, she raises it high, until it catches the light--and slices it to ribbons.<br /> <br /> Silver is torn apart into red and yellow and orange and green and blue and violet, the beams sliding and slipping over one another like a kaleidoscope. Given a moment, they piece themselves into a regal figure, a woman no less than nine feet tall, her severe features framed in a halo of shimmering color-knives.<br /> <br /> Emerging from a billowing sleeve, her hand is little more than a collection of armaments, archaic and modern, but all lethally edged. Even the night breeze is cut apart by her touch. She does not speak, for even her words would slice the head from Aria's shoulders.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am... tired, of being a castle wall. Enduring endless punishment and holding that which is precious to me, and... helpless, when my defenses are found wanting. I must become capable of... sortie. A blade unsheathed to take that which is rightfully mine, and punish thieves with the taking of their hand.&quot; Her hollow jags, unable to completely hide her aggression here in her own heart-of-hearts.<br /> <br /> The Lady of Blades inclines her head, and thrusts her hand into Aria's empty face, shredding whispers and darkness like gauze. But one of her fingers pulls away, swallowed into the void, and Aria awakens in Markus' workshop, feeling a metallic chill coiled between her lungs. <i>And so my principles weaken once more.</i></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Radioheart smiles at Umbra. Then he breathes in deeply, eyes closed and the electronic displays on his clothes showing luminous lines of cardiac rhythm. He is afraid, but the fear no longer controls him. Much like Umbra opening the doors of her errant heart with a certain Mind spell, Radioheart smiles at Noose.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Here comes the sun, do, dun, do, do / Here comes the sun, and I say / It's all right&quot;</i> He begins steadily, measuring his tone with caution so as to not startle Noose and to leave room for a crescendo. Noose is impassive and unresponsive, his cybernetic eyes glazing over.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Little darling, it's been a long cold lonely winter / Little darling, it feels like years since it's been here&quot;</i> He continues, tapping his feet and doing little cheerful finger-snaps. Noose ever so slowly imitates the gesture, even though his rhythm is terribly off-key and his skeletal hands make an ugly and unpleasant noise. Radioheart is not perturbed nor annoyed, and in fact picks up speed to encourage Noose.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Sun, sun, sun, here it comes...&quot;</i> Radioheart gets up and does a flourish with his hands, taking the sunlight pouring from the nearest window and shaping it into a stylized and smiling sun. Noose makes an expression of confusion, as if saying &quot;I did not know you could do that&quot;.<br /> <br /> Radioheart understands the non-verbal message despite his neural issues, and shrugs as if to say &quot;I didn't know either until recently&quot;.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Little darling, I feel that ice is slowly melting / Little darling, it seems like years since it's been clear Here comes the sun, do, dun, do, do / Here comes the sun, and I say / It's all right&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Radioheart walks to Noose and gives the deformed and deranged man a kiss on the forehead.<br /> <br /> Noose looks even more confused. &quot;... my brother never did any of this for me,&quot; Noose observed, not quite crying but visibly disillusioned.<br /> <br /> &quot;I can be your new brother, if you want!&quot; Radioheart smiled, all the resentment in the past.<br /> <br /> &quot;Now that was quick.&quot; Umbra's glad that that is working out thus far, and smiles at them both.<br /> <br /> &quot;What can I say? I was built to do this,&quot; He boasts.<br /> <br /> &quot;...you know, I was built too,&quot; Confessed Noose.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wh-- what?&quot; Said Radioheart with great puzzlement.<br /> <br /> &quot;I came into this world fully formed, grown in a metal womb beneath the earth. You were given the knowledge of love and art, I was given the knowledge of death and destruction. Even now, I keep thinking of a hundred thousand ways to kill both of you, and I don't like it anymore.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;As you move, your perspective changes. Have you ever tried creating something of beauty?&quot; \u2014 Umbra pushes a drawing crayon and a sheet of paper to them across the table.<br /> <br /> He tentatively takes the crayon and paper. With laborious effort and a shaking hand, Noose draws a very simple flower. The entire process takes a full minute, and he is visibly fighting the urge to draw tanks, trenches and worse things still. He pushes his childlike scribble forward, looking expectant.<br /> <br /> &quot;Good, it's a first step. It was hard, wasn't it? You should feel accomplished, but don't stop.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Thank you. My head hurts immensely, but I think it is a good pain. By the way, Radioheart?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sorry for hurting you so much for so long. I wasn't thinking straight.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I forgive you, as long as you don't go back to who you used to be.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;ADA, turn off the lights! And put a projector on Scarab the moment Daedalus enters the room!&quot; Krieger gestures. &quot;Everyone else - silence!&quot;<br /> <br /> ADA immediately complies, and the Scarab fidgets with the tie of his improvised suit. Radioheart gives him an enthusiastic thumbs-up and whispers &quot;you can do it, I believe in you!&quot;. There is a moment of profound silence when Daedalus and Scarab finally meet face to face once more. The faint sounds of technology appear to be much louder, and time crawls to a snail's pace. Clara almost yells <i>SURPRISE!</i> but instead fetches a bag of napkins with impressive speed. Triage and Noose stay a bit to the side, not being accustomed to family reunions and not wishing to get in the way.<br /> <br /> &quot;...Scarab? What happened to you? Are you hurt? Did you-- did you do this to yourself?&quot; Asked Daedalus, approaching with considerable trepidation but also visible concern. His usual facade of the imperturbable Germanic chemist was quickly falling apart.<br /> <br /> &quot;I did, Daedalus, but I am not hurt. Just... a little out of touch, it seems,&quot; Scarab tentatively extends his many arthropod limbs for a hug. &quot;How's my brilliant apprentice doing? Have you joined a Legacy yet, maybe adopted a son?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No no no. I am the one who has been completely out of touch. I should have visited you in person a lot more. Master, I joined the Forged Masters almost a decade ago, and I have always turned down opportunities to raise a family. I did not realize your mind was... in such disrepair. I should have sent more than just drones, I am so, so sorry.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's OK, we still have a lot of time to fix ourselves and the world. Come here and hug me, or we're gonna stand around for nothing and get rusty,&quot; Scarab jokes.<br /> <br /> Master and apprentice embrace each other, and the sound of clockwork hearts beating together can be heard by everyone witnessing the reunion, like a melody in High Speech.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-13-2022, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T08:31:15-08:00","id":1499650,"title":"","content":"More stuff, y'all. Comments and questions are very welcome!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Liz approaches the drone quickly, refusing to break eye contact. \u201cMm, they just left you didn\u2019t they? Guess that\u2019s the problem!working together with solitary creatures, isn\u2019t it? Which data pillar is yours, hm?\u201d Lifting its crumpled head, Liz retrieves what is for all intents and purposes a diminutive car jack mounted perpendicularly to a ratcheting press, attached to which is a long, slender crochet hook and a magnifying glass.<br /> <br /> \u201cCome on now, let\u2019s get you back to your hive..\u201d Liz begins slowly ratcheting its skull plates apart. It is not a clean operation. Placing her eye to the eyepiece, she positions the hook in a manner she deems satisfactory, and plunges in, rotating the hook slightly, before swiftly retracting it. Grasped within the hook is a minuscule, 150 micrometer strand of something, softly pulsing with energy.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can show me. I\u2019m a friend. You must spend a lot of time upkeeping it; I\u2019m sure you have the best hive in \u2014It\u2019s eyes are still moving, right? Okay, good.\u201d<br /> <br /> With reverence, Liz reaches into the chamber of her gun, and removes the payload. Sticking the dart in her mouth, she slides open the dump valve, and allows the pressurized liquid to flow in. She then unscrews the needle from the dart, placing it in her mouth. Moving extremely slowly, she \u2018pecks\u2019 it into the strand, and blows the solution through the needle, using her tongue to monitor flow. Finally, she moves away, spitting the needle and excess solution. Her pupils briefly dilate asymmetrically, before remembering they\u2019re not supposed to and returning to normal.<br /> <br /> \u201cokay.\u201d She groans. \u201cThat\u2019ll work.\u201d<br /> <br /> After the gruesome biomechanical lobotomy is finished, the wasp-drone whirs and snaps back to attention and full function, its compound eyeballs now glowing the same neon-green as the mind control fluid. It observes the Genii in a calm and patient manner, as if awaiting verbal commands.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Liz can feel the machine's focus is turned on her. For a mere fraction of a second, every hair on her body rises, her blood slows to a crawl, and her pupils shrink as the universe dilates.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Shit.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The laser comes not as a long, sluggish ray of collimated energy, but as a single cloud-shaking thunderclap. The air itself ignites, sweeping her off her feet with a deafening shockwave as the air collapses around her. Her nose, lips, and hair are immolated outright, reduced to vapors. Her ears, useless and destroyed, leak blood and fluid. Where once she had eyes, now rest unrecognizable discs of charred mucus. It is impossible to tell whether or not her clothing has survived, as her torso has been reduced to one unbroken, tangled mass of loose, ablated skin, and fire.<br /> <br /> Somehow, impossibly, beyond all reason or mercy, she remains conscious, desperately, agonizingly clawing for a treatment she knows is there, with no sense of sight, sound, or touch.<br /> <br /> Through a combination of muscle memory, dumb luck, and bad safety culture, Liz accidentally stabs herself in the finger while flailing around! This allows the slip-ring on the needle to come fully off, dumping the contents into the narrow confines of her finger. Because of this, it is significantly less effective than it would be normally.<br /> <br /> Targeting 'important' areas first such as the eyes, inner ears, and arms, Liz's body boils and writhes. The smell of burning fat, sugar and hair is soon drowned out by the unmistakable stench of crushed ants. As the lungs are repaired, they begin operating, accelerating the rate of mend. The fat from her body recedes unnaturally. Charred skin is absorbed back into her body, sinking in like steel on ice. Then her clothes. Then the syringe itself.<br /> <br /> Her new eyes flick open. Painblockers do nothing to alleviate the mental discomfort of sitting up half-skinless, emaciated.<br /> <br /> Slowly, slowly, she reaches for something. A weapon. A tool. Anything.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u201cWell, I\u2019d better get to work then.\u201d Cousteau pops another sugar (sugar?) cube into his mouth, and steps out.<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t take long before he returns, a garbage bag slung over each shoulder, and a thick spatula in hand.<br /> <br /> Cousteau sets the bags on the table, and tears them open, revealing piles of very heavily sedated seabirds. Their wings flop at odd angles, and as Cousteau uses his spatula to flip and flop them into the \u2018recovery position\u2019, they don\u2019t react, remaining limp and malleable.<br /> <br /> \u201cI could do with some jars\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Hypatia tries not to giggle at the sighs of a man handling birds with a spatula. &quot;Would cans of paint work? I think I saw a couple empty ones around here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hypatia retrieves the small paint-cans.<br /> <br /> \u201cHm. Not ideal, but, I can make it work.\u201d<br /> <br /> Cousteau snaps on his gloves, and grabs one of the larger birds. \u201cDo you fit in a paint can?\u201d He asks the bird. \u201cMaybe not, I might have to do you large fellows in sections.\u201d<br /> <br /> &quot;Let me just work with these a bit.&quot; Hypatia takes her cans to one of the workshops and gets to work. A handfull of minutes later, Hypatia comes back with much smaller cans, just the right size to hold a sparrow inside them.<br /> <br /> &quot;What is the difference between a raven and a writing desk?&quot; \u2014 River muses quietly, watching senior Cousteau work.<br /> <br /> &quot;Two legs versus four.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u201cAha! Now that is much more efficient.\u201d<br /> <br /> Reaching under his shirt, he retrieves several flasks of god-doesn\u2019t-want-to-know-what, and pours varying amounts of them into the cans.<br /> <br /> \u201c...dipping things in stuff...\u201d he mutters under his breath, tossing in five of his sugar cubes to each.<br /> <br /> The liquid inside the containers is a friendly dull pink, and seems to have grown quite viscous. Cousteau smiles with satisfaction, and grabs the first sparrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry, little friend. You won\u2019t remember a thing.\u201d He promises, placing the bird into the can.<br /> <br /> Adding the very wide-band sensor (truly an advanced, but ultimately very boring, piece of machinery), the container comes right up to the point of overflowing.<br /> <br /> Squinting critically,Cousteau spits in it, before re-sealing the can.<br /> <br /> He performs similar operations with all the available birds, stopping every now and again to shake, invert, heat, cool, or tap on them.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou must remind them what it is they\u2019re supposed to be doing in there\u201d he explains. \u201cThe little ones can be forgetful of their genetic code, you know.\u201d</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Markus takes a long, deep breath. &quot;I understand. Now, let us begin.&quot;<br /> <br /> Markus has Aria place her entire left arm into a steel cage dotted with screws. By turning the screws until they <i>just</i> make contact with Aria's skin, Markus records a variety of measurements, before flagging down Caesar and Matilda. The three work surprisingly well as a team; heating, shaping, and machining steel with a fine degree of precision. Matilda, blades in a whirl, seems to take a worrying amount of joy from carving wood, perhaps seeing it as somehow surgery-adjacent.<br /> <br /> As Markus puts the finishing touches on the items (an engraving on the cylinder of the revolver depicting Cain mowing down a field of cartoonish zombies with a very unstable looking flamethrower, and a clean oval meant to represent Aria's void etched across the blade of the knife, respectively), he remembers.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah <i>fuck.</i> The <i>traps</i>!&quot;<br /> <br /> Exploding into action, Markus practically knocks over Caesar (though such a feat would be impressive) as he reaches for associated tools, scrap, and steel. Matilda and Caesar move to help, and, together, they begin practically overflowing the limited floor space with an assortment of traps. Most are very simple: a salvaged bear trap, a .50 BMG round in a tube with a nail under the primer, an assortment of Matilda-spun thread (food-safe and biodegradable!) that when disturbed would drop a 480 pound counterweight, fastening like a lasso and ripping the ankle of whatever unlucky bastard stepped into it high into the air, and the old-fashioned &quot;bent branch&quot; trap, redone with leaf-spring suspension and massive hollow-ground spikes.<br /> <br /> &quot;If we keep this up for much longer, we won't be able to fit it all in the car!&quot; Markus comments, finalizing the latching mechanism on an enormous rectangular bear trap, designed to pinch a human-sized target's throat. &quot;Speaking of, what ever happened to that disgusting crustbucket of an engine you found? We should put 'er in the car before we go!&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">After informing the Pixel Trinity about recent events, the Cabal carefully transports the Cicada-Cryptid in its crate back to the Sanctum. On the way there, the creature wakes up and starts making buzzing noises, as if distressed from being in a dark and unfamiliar environment. Upon the crate being opened via crowbar, the creature pokes its eyes and antennae out of the box, and looks at its surroundings as if confused. It turns its attention to Telos, and waves at him with one of its insect paws. It jumps out of the crate and onto the table, picking up some of Telos' tools, feeling them and nibbling on them, then putting the tools back into place. For now, the creature doesn't seem hostile at all, though it is safe to assume it might cause problems if left unsupervised.<br /> <br /> Camus looks it over carefully, fascinated by its biology and appearance.<br /> <br /> Telos returns the wave, and turns to watch it nibble on a hammer, making a note to test that one just in case. He rests his chin in his palm, pensive. Sound...<br /> <br /> Telos gets up from his chair to follow the critter, corralling it in his hands briefly. Long enough to speak to it of the salamander, of the hair and fingernail, in High Speech. Given the schematics, the purpose behind such things, the Cicada's chitin responds in kind, partaking long enough to grow several break-away scales, perfect for sampling.<br /> <br /> Camus doesn't waste time, beginning a routine look through Telos' microscope - and breaking into a grin when he realizes he got the perfect sample, no damage at all, perfect for sketching and taking notes.<br /> <br /> Breaking off another scale, Telos lays it out on his workbench like a watch. Flipping his hammer around to the narrow end, he taps at it gently, as if molding gold into a new shape. As he does, he speaks to it of how purpose suffuses a thing, even as individual parts have their own functions.<br /> <br /> The purpose of a hammer is to drive, break, and bend, but is that the purpose of the handle? Perhaps. Yet if you had just a handle, people would say its purpose was for holding things. Thus.<br /> <br /> By the end of it, he's got a stretch of the Cicada's vocal chords resting gingerly on a bit of sterile cloth.<br /> <br /> Camus goes to work as soon as he's done, delicately preparing them for their purpose...which is made significantly easier by his notes. By the end of it, he's made something he thinks could serve a place in a ritual spell, especially for animal communication.<br /> <br /> Telos looks it over with a quiet 'hmm,' turning to his pile of spare parts, eventually finding an old radio transmitter. More work with his hammer, and soon the two devices are one. He powers it on, fiddling with knobs and levers until the chords make some of the Cicada's strange warbling, rising and falling, chittering, before he turns it off, satisfied.<br /> <br /> The Cicada is likely quite confused, like a dog hearing humans pretend to bark.<br /> <br /> &quot;It'll take some field testing, but this is the basic prototype; once we have the patterns down, I can use a smaller transmitter in the final product.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Indeed. I look forward to the work process; it'll be a fascinating excursion.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Assuming we're not attacked by bigfeet. ... bigfoots?&quot; Telos inclines his head in thought, his quiet nature returning as the rush of the work fades.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think it would be bigfeet. Or sasquatches.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Umbra drives to Portal, engaging in a rapid-fire exchange of messages with the local manager. Soon, she arrives, changing out into one of the light-up rave suits she stores at the premises for surprise shows.<br /> <br /> Soon, she's blazing through the steps, highlighted by multicolored strobes, her every move translated to several connected plasma screens, as ESM blasts out of the speakers.<br /> <br /> Energy wells behind her eyes with the last beats of the song, as her will triggers the smoke engines and she lets herself step back into the Thura.<br /> <br /> Upon the climax of the spectacularly energetic dance, Umbra fades into the smoke cloud and dematerializes like a polygonal model in an archaic video game. For a brief but suspenseful moment, she is without any frame of reference for her surroundings due to lacking a physical form. The only sensation is a like being submerged in the depths of the ocean without a diving suit, but with binary codes instead of water molecules. The horrid cold of the oceanic abyss is replaced by a cybernetic euphoria, which is focused like a hundred-terawatt laser as Umbra gets closer and closer at an accelerated rhythm.<br /> <br /> She is one with the electrical currents, moving through a dazzling and glowing tunnel of data with the colors of her Synthwave-Praxis. She emerges as a sphere of luminous butterflies wrapped in Pandemonic chains, soon expanding into her natural infomorph configuration. Urakiri is with her, ready to slice through anything in her way like a futuristic plasma torch. The adrenaline and satisfaction are so intense that it takes a few seconds for her to notice she is on the top of a vast spiral construct of neon green and blue, like a radio communication tower.<br /> <br /> Due to her level of talent with Forces, she need not fear a sudden fall, but the vista is nonetheless absolutely staggering. She can just barely make out a sort of cyberpunk district below, with various Supernal Denizens zooming everywhere and dancing with each other to exchange information. Despite being a Mastigos, the music is quite simply Heaven to her ears. The sky above is eternally nocturnal and filled with ever-shifting constellations that reflect humanity's hopes and dreams for a future that never was achieved, but will become reality through the Gnosis and Wisdom of Umbra.<br /> <br /> Umbra deduces from the particularly retro-futuristic aesthetics of the architecture and entities that she is within a sort of downtown/central district, roughly analogous to Manhattan in NYC or West End in London. From here, Ricardo's map shows 4 other adjacent regions:<br /> <br /> 1) Northward is the Crypto-Currency District. Polygonal and drone-like constructs fly at eardrum-shattering speeds between here and there, carrying valuable packages of digital wealth away from the eyes of most governmental oversight.<br /> <br /> 2) Southward is the Social Media District, resembling an untamed jungle of venomous opinions, camouflaged fake news and the occasional golden flower of revolutionary social insight.<br /> <br /> 3) Eastward is the Gaming District, shaped like a Roman Coliseum made out of intertwined and vein-like cables which coalesce into a massive pulsating heart that occupies a looming electro-tower. The sounds of competition are thunderous and the cybernetic body parts of gladiators are torn off and sent flying through the air by the hundreds every minute.<br /> <br /> 4) Westward is the Darkweb District. The map cuts off around the entrance, which is a rusty and corroded elevator swaying back and forth ominously over a crimson and foul-smelling mist of human depravity and malice.<br /> <br /> Umbra smiles, as she moves to scale the tower down. It's time to get to business. As she swings down, lightly jumping through the twisting of the electronic rebar, she eyes the gaming district \u2014 but then looks to the Darkweb.<br /> <br /> Soon, she is at the ground floor, and she begins walking. Electronic vehicles flit past her, as she makes her way towards the living, beating heart-hubs of the transporting and commerce within this digital world. Within this world, she's an actinic blue vision, given tangible form by the underlying matter-body within her Pattern.<br /> <br /> Here, the injects come light and easy, as the world is more receptive to her will. <i>\u2014 run gnosis engine designate:Umbra exec WE ARE THE MUSIC-MAKERS /</i>. She looks around, trying to make sense of where she can obtain transportation of her own.<br /> <br /> Umbra notices via her Forces Knowing spell that her cellphone works analogously to how it does inside baseline reality: it can be used as an omni-equipment to interface with various key-points and special devices, which are now clearly highlighted by auras of butterflies. Umbra also discovers a holographic price list hovering near a sort of bus-stop, which reads as follows:<br /> <br /> <i>1 Mana For Low-Rhythm Inter-District Travel<br /> <br /> 2 Mana For High-Rhythm Inter-District Travel<br /> <br /> +1 Surcharge For Beta-Class Personalized Transportation<br /> <br /> +2 Surcharge For Alpha-Class Personalized Transportation</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>[ACCESS TO DARKWEB DISTRICT: UNAVAILABLE UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE]</b></i></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-14-2022, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T16:05:57-08:00","id":1499987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488771-your-moments-of-awesome-epic-fails-tearful-sadness-and-noodle-incidents?p=1499490#post1499490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Huntsman tries to move toward Matilda, but cannot even move past a few inches before collapsing. Its entire body has been molten and incinerated so thoroughly that it does not even have flesh anymore, only a wooden doll-like skeleton. Gordon makes his way toward the feeble and agonizing creature, licking his lips and rubbing his hands in anticipation. The Huntsman tries to wobble away, but lacks the muscles and ligaments to move properly and lets out a quiet, gurgling scream.<br /> <br /> Gordon picks up the Huntsman by the throat and makes the fey creature look him in the eyes. &quot;Any last words?&quot; He inquires in a jolly tone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, nooooo... are you going to kill me? I'm sooo scared...&quot; The Huntsman manages to pathetically cough.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nope! I'm going to make you wish you were dead, my <i>most exotic and delectable of meals!</i> Don't worry, no part of you will go to waste!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait, NO! Eat the soldiers, not me, PLEASE!&quot; The Huntsman is dragged into Gordon's ravenous, gaping maw. The horrid, abominable sight can only be described as the painting of Saturn Devouring His Son brought to life. Even the Rat Pack, having seen Arcadia and the Gentry, feel as though their grip on reality loosens ever so slightly from merely gazing upon the mockery of a smile that Gordon does as he goes about the grisly act.<br /> <br /> And after the blink of an eye, the Huntsman is gone. All the remaining toy soldiers look at Gordon, petrified with terror. Gordon gives Caesar a knowing and satisfied look, before staring at the enemies and raising his voice.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Fee-fi-fo-fum, </i><br /> <i>I smell the blood of an Englishman, </i><br /> <i>Be he alive, or be he dead, </i><br /> <i>I'll grind his bones to make my bread!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> All of the enemies immediately flee into the Thorns without looking back.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so if I had to take a guess, Gordon is either a Changeling of the Gristlegrinder Kith (and, subsequently, the Ogre Seeming, if this was in 1st Ed C:tL), or a Beast with the 'Skin Deep' Atavism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T16:42:51-08:00","id":1499990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488771-your-moments-of-awesome-epic-fails-tearful-sadness-and-noodle-incidents?p=1499987#post1499987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so if I had to take a guess, Gordon is either a Changeling of the Gristlegrinder Kith (and, subsequently, the Ogre Seeming, if this was in 1st Ed C:tL), or a Beast with the 'Skin Deep' Atavism.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. Anakim Predator with Changelings as Kin, and he was using the Ravenous Maw Atavism. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T10:43:11-08:00","id":1500056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488771-your-moments-of-awesome-epic-fails-tearful-sadness-and-noodle-incidents?p=1499990#post1499990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter. Anakim Predator with Changelings as Kin, and he was using the Ravenous Maw Atavism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, shoulda' known that it was that particular Atavism. Though, admittedly, it's been a while since I went over them, so my memory regarding them was as fuzzy as one could expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T16:25:41-08:00","id":1504228,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Inkblot guides the Rat Pack through the Dreaming Road, distancing himself from the curiously peaceful neighborhood into the seedy underbelly. The detour is uncomfortably long, and gradually inflicts a sense of creeping dread as the details of the scenery twist and deform. Detached shadows crawl around and whisper gibberish that drips with violent intent. The gas lamps' illumination takes on a lurid crimson hue and the temperature drops sharply, with the visible gusts of air from the Changelings' mouths also becoming that color. There is no more jaunty comedic music, only the steady echoing of dripping and scratching. After what seems like an eternity, they arrive at what appears to be the ruins of a hospital. The dripping and scratching noises are louder now, and the Changelings can smell a horrible wave of the ferric scent associated with blood.<br /> <br /> Ever so cautiously, they enter the hospital. There is seemingly no one there, and no massive blood stains as one would expect. But the noises, they are very loud now, as if they are one corridor away from finding whoever this entity might be. Even Inkblot seems to hesitate and fidget, as if fearing the worse for everyone involved if things go wrong. He motions for the Rat Pack to hear him whisper, his Mien all the more gruesome in the crimson light.<br /> <br /> &quot;Whatever happens, do NOT try to fight him, I beg you,&quot; With that last warning, he knocks on the door, which slowly opens on its own. They see a humanoid figure with filth-encrusted and blade-like fingernails parting the tissues of a rotten carcass. Bloodshot, rheumy eyes fail to register any of you, swollen like overripe grapes. A red cloak, once proud, now little more than a rag stained with the viscera of past conquests. As you enter, absolute silence falls onto the room. A finger ceases its skittering movement across the body's veins.<br /> <br /> Aria's mien makes it relatively easy to hide her surprise, at least. The rim of her hollow curdles briefly, and she inclines her head. In the crimson, the whispers of her face take on a metallic edge. &quot;Charmed. Would you prefer we conduct this business with or without names?&quot;<br /> <br /> Cain steps next to Aria, his curiosity outweighing whatever self preservation instincts he has. \u201cSymbolism, remember? Maybe approaching it with a gesture of good faith might work better than words.\u201d<br /> <br /> Cain takes out his flask, and offers it to the man.<br /> <br /> Markus, for his part, busies himself with mentally cataloguing every item in the room, double-checking each one.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for him, there aren\u2019t many, and he\u2019s soon forced to find other things to draw his attention away from the raw spectacle.<br /> <br /> Sanguine gives a brief and annoyed glance to the Changelings, as if they were things he would scrape off his shoes. He wordlessly makes a dismissive gesture toward them, and refocuses on the grisly and cryptic surgery.<br /> <br /> Leilani gracefully fails to grasp the severity of the scenario, though she knows something must be dead in close vicinity and their conversation partner must be particularly hard to reach.<br /> <br /> Hmh. Aria takes a step closer, circling around once she's pretty sure she's found the least in-the-way spot to stand, hands folding behind her back. A lean forward, 'looking' the surgery up and down. After a pregnant moment, she speaks a quiet, genuine, &quot;artistry, isn't it?My studies were in the psychological rather than the physiological, but even there we learned how much of what we consider 'us' lives in those vessels.&quot; Here in the dream, her attention is palpable, a shadow that the mind can sense even if the eyes do not, 'looking' up at Sanguine. &quot;What do you see, in this forest of rubies?&quot; Her tone is low, attentive, drawing to mind whispers in a library or over a bottle of wine.<br /> <br /> &quot;Artistry and science, in mystic matrimony. I appreciate that you don't recoil so easily at the sight of my handiwork. As for what I see... all of us who cleave to humanity still bleed red. My grand strategy is simply to make that perfectly apparent. A standardized genetic blueprint, with phenotypical expressions guided not by random sequencing of DNA, but by the Pneuma inherent to us all and carried within our vital fluids. Have a seat, all of you. What brings you here? You have my curiosity, do not waste it. My work is very important to me, and you're postponing universal transcendence of biological divisions if your business is trivially handled by someone else.&quot;<br /> <br /> While Leilani is sure of her ability to appeal to these bloody sensibilities, Aria seems like she has a particular handle on the situation.<br /> <br /> Aria inclines her head, having to run that through some dusty Latin picked up in med school. But she does find somewhere to sit, trusting in the motley to do likewise. &quot;We're in need of a heart. Conjured meat--even should we be capable of that ourselves--is insufficient. We're wresting the symbolic life of it out of the hands of the Kindly Ones.&quot;<br /> <br /> A beat. &quot;It must be more the patient's heart than his own flesh and blood.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Whatever happens, do NOT try to fight him, I beg you,&quot; Inkblot's plea rings in Cain's ears. Despite how highly he regards himself in most scenarios, avoiding fights is the one place where he will concede, just a bit. He'll let Aria handle this one.<br /> <br /> &quot;How does that advance my own projects, pray tell?&quot; He inquires, with his tone implying that he is far too obsessed with whatever lofty goals he just ranted about to properly conceive of making effort for anything else.<br /> <br /> It might have been that easy. Alas. A moment's consideration. &quot;You wish universal transcendence of biological division; then your foe is not solely cells and sinew. There are beings who lay claim to the bodies of common humanity.&quot;<br /> <br /> A vague gesture to her own disfigured mien, briefly remembering the feel of her Keeper's fingers sinking in to scoop her face out. It curls the rim of her hollow into short-lived fangs. &quot;You will have to usurp them and their claims, if you wish to free all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Perhaps due to her curse, Leilani feels a draw to appease him. Having never taken a seat -- in part because of the awkward job of fumbling for one without the attendance of Aria's helping hand, caught as she were in other dealings -- Leilani takes a step forward towards the smell she is at this point positive must be a corpse, though in the dreamland she's unsure if there is even license to take moral qualms. Can corpses come from nowhere here? It would make as much sense as anything else, she supposes.<br /> <br /> Her approach is met with a wall. Not a physical wall, but a wall of presence. A refusal of her approach, metaphysical as it were. She detects no mistake in her step, no faux pas in her mannerisms, and yet her curse doesn't do enough legwork to penetrate this surgeon's mistrust and solitude. Even the slight limp and faint dampness added to her clothes seems to have made little affect on him. The rules are different here, Leilani understands, though she's unsure how much of it is the dream and how much is him. Wordlessly, she redirects herself. Further from the table, she makes it look like she had no intention of approach anyhow. Restless legs, she states with her gait. Nothing more. Ignore me.<br /> <br /> Sanguine slowly approaches Aria, and looks her dead in the &quot;eyes&quot;. He is unbothered by the phantasmagorical whispers that emanate from within Aria's void, and indeed seems to be eerily curious about how it works.<br /> <br /> &quot;How do you process sensory data without the relevant organs? Do you need to eat, drink, breathe, sleep, excrete? How can you even think when a large portion of your frontal lobe is missing along with your face? Can you get pregnant and sustain a fetus if you cannot transfer nutrients and oxygen to it? If an object is inserted in that orifice, where does it go?&quot;<br /> <br /> The blood-sorcerer speaks in a completely clinical tone, and clearly does not care in the slightest if his questions are inappropriate or invasive. &quot;That's all quite fascinating to me, really. Relevant to my research, as well. I cannot allow humanity to end up like you. Give me a written document with detailed answers within seven days, and I'll prepare the metaphysical component of that clockwork heart.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is the gulf between Sanguine and Aria. The void of her hollow stretches for a tiny infinity to separate his vulgar dissection from the holistic approach on which she prides herself. Aria cannot afford to reduce her patients to pieces of anatomy and connective tissue; Sanguine does not--can not?--see anything but.<br /> <br /> She meets his stare in her own way, feeling the iron in her soul creeping its way up her spine, a blade threatening to unsheathe. What color do you bleed, o' sage of carmine? Is it any more vital than the liquid light which coursed through my Keeper? These thoughts rise no higher than that, however, failing to escape the darkness where her secrets live.<br /> <br /> &quot;Provide an address. I will have the documents overnight.&quot; Conspicuous neutrality, better than feigned geniality. Show Sanguine that discomfort and hate do not control you.<br /> <br /> &quot;Understood. I will have the item delivered to your Hollow around the same time. Now be gone from my sight, all of you. My work requires focus,&quot; He makes another dismissive gesture towards the Changelings, and then turns his back to them.<br /> <br /> Inkblot is suddenly possessed by a rage completely uncharacteristic of a Victorian alienist. He forcibly spins Sanguine around so the blood-sorcerer is looking him in his moonlight-eyes and horrid smile of barely contained violent intent.<br /> <br /> &quot;Have you not a speck of bedside manners, sir? You might be working for the betterment of humanity, and though Aria might no longer be fully human, she is still a person! She has thoughts and feelings just like you do, even if buried beneath obsession and arrogance! You would do well to respect the boundaries of those you work with from now on, because if you don't, you will have to answer to me. And I have ways of dealing with butchers like you. Goodbye, Sanguine, and may you examine your flaws with the same dedication you have for others' flaws before it's too late.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sanguine completely ignores Inkblot and returns to his dissection.<br /> <br /> Leilani winces, inwardly and silently.<br /> <br /> Cain scoots away from Inkblot, wanting to be far away from the chaos.<br /> <br /> \u201cUh, well, \u2026 he doesn\u2019t speak for all of us. Excuse his manners, please.\u201d Cain says the last part through gritted teeth, and grabs the collar of Inkblot\u2019s shirt. \u201cYou\u2019re putting Aria in danger. Suck it up, or else someone\u2019s gonna end up killed.\u201d He whispers to the psychiatrist.<br /> <br /> Aria gets to her feet, cursing herself. I knew Inkblot was under duress-- The moment of terror passes without Inkblot erupting into a fine mist, and she hurries over to shepherd the motley out, fetching Leilani on the way.<br /> <br /> Assuming they're not avasculated or otherwise stopped, she doesn't relent until the group is back out on the cobbles and the door shut behind them. A moment to catch her breath. &quot;L-Leilani. If you would be so kind as to... sing a song while we make our way back, please.&quot;<br /> <br /> A lingering 'look' at Inkblot. &quot;I appreciate it, truly,&quot; an affectionate tone.<br /> <br /> Cain looks at Inkblot and huffs. Stupid motherfucker almost got us all killed. Is it that hard to sit down and shut up?<br /> <br /> &quot;U-uh, sure.&quot; Leilani clears her throat, and begins to hum, hoping to not draw too much attention in the streets but still please the ears of her motley.<br /> <br /> Inkblot ignores Cain entirely, and instead focuses on guiding the Rat Pack back to Ironside.\u200b</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec